1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,050
Our radio then reported seismic activity near a volcano.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,988
An earthquake might make it unsafe to stay.

3
00:00:06,988 --> 00:00:13,238
Scientists were studying magma with a thermodynamic model, but nobody knew whether the volcano would erupt.

4
00:00:13,238 --> 00:00:15,977
We followed the teachers to a safe building.

5
00:00:15,977 --> 00:00:21,943
There, a poster showed how a tsunami, an avalanche, a drought or flooding could become a disaster.

6
00:00:21,943 --> 00:00:25,806
A torrent outside reminded us that water could be destructive.

7
00:00:25,806 --> 00:00:29,636
I dropped my bag: a small mishap, not a calamity.

8
00:00:29,636 --> 00:00:34,545
Ignoring warnings could endanger everyone and jeopardise our return,’ Mira said.

9
00:00:34,545 --> 00:00:37,852
A careless choice can have catastrophic results.

10
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:41,181
When we finally got home, I opened my notebook.

11
00:00:41,181 --> 00:00:44,227
Now I could remember every word through our trip.

